The ``current``, ``current_range`` and ``current_limit`` parameters of the ``YokogawaGS200``,
and its ``measure`` parameter in voltage source mode, now use the unit ``A`` instead of ``I``.
The ``ramp_rate`` and ``ramp_step`` parameters now start with the units ``A/s`` and ``A``
instead of ``V/s`` and ``V`` if the instrument is in current source mode when connecting, as
they already did after changing the source mode.

``YokogawaGS200Monitor.delay`` (``measure.delay``) is now in seconds, the unit the instrument
uses, instead of ms. The value was already sent to the instrument unconverted, so
``delay(500)`` set a delay of 500 s despite the ``ms`` unit. The parameter now accepts values
from 0 to 999.999 s in steps of 1 ms, e.g. ``delay(0.5)`` for 500 ms, and returns the delay
as a ``float`` in seconds instead of an ``int`` rounded to whole seconds.
